      <VERS vnumber="15"> He hath <gr str="7646">filled </gr>me with <gr str="4844">bitterness</gr>, he hath made me <gr str="7301">drunken </gr>with <gr str="3939">wormwood</gr>. </VERS>
      <VERS vnumber="16"> He hath also <gr str="1638">broken </gr>my <gr str="8127">teeth </gr>with gravel <gr str="2687">stones</gr>, he hath <gr str="3728">covered </gr>me with <gr str="665">ashes</gr>. </VERS>
      <VERS vnumber="17"> And thou hast removed my soul far <gr str="2186 5315">off </gr>from <gr str="4480 7965">peace</gr>: I <gr str="5382">forgot </gr>
        <gr str="2896">prosperity</gr>. </VERS>
      <VERS vnumber="18"> And I <gr str="559">said</gr>, My <gr str="5331">strength </gr>and my <gr str="8431">hope </gr>is <gr str="6">perished </gr>from the <gr str="4480 3068">LORD</gr>: </VERS>
      <VERS vnumber="19">
        <gr str="2142">Remembering </gr>mine <gr str="6040">affliction </gr>and my <gr str="4788">misery</gr>, the <gr str="3939">wormwood </gr>and the <gr str="7219">gall</gr>. </VERS>
      <VERS vnumber="20"> My <gr str="5315">soul </gr>hath <STYLE css="color:#808080;font-style:italic"> them </STYLE> still in <gr str="2142 2142">remembrance</gr>, and is <gr str="7743">humbled </gr>
